* Lamp-lit places lit (openc2e Creatures 2 project, our own script; owner,
* 2026-11-26: "search the map for room sprites that indicate the presence of
* light, and suggest what the corresponding light levels should be", then
* "A and B"). Run by openc2e after the world loads (Additions folder); safe
* to repeat. Named to run last: additions run in name order, and some
* reshape rooms (pool.cos, lift.cos), so light set before them went to the
* room as it was before.
*
* The world file's light (LITE) for many rooms does not match their art:
* rooms painted with lamps, lamplight or glowing lava at light 0-71, and
* three lamp-lit rooms with a negative light source (-106), which our
* daylight treats as no lamp. Each room below gets the light its picture
* shows. A light source (LSRC above 0) marks a lamp: the room keeps its
* light at night (World::tickDaylight, SkyTint), as the incubator's do.
* Light also matters to creatures: darkness makes every species sleepy,
* and cave germs keep to dark rooms.
*
* For each room a helper object is made at a point inside it (checked to
* be in that room alone), sets its light (LITE is the light of TARG's
* room), and goes.

inst
* lamps painted, the room dark or dimmed at night
* two hanging lamps (room 155: was 9, light source 0)
new: simp blnk 1 0 0 0 setv attr 16 mvto 6971 1322 setv lite 150 setv lsrc 1 kill targ
